    "With the correction, Larry has:\n\n- Cats: \\(3\\)\n- Dogs: \\(4 \\times 3 = 12\\)\n- Cats and dogs total: \\(3+12=15\\)\n\nLet the number of fish be \\(f\\). Then the number of gerbils is \\(\\frac{f}{3}\\), so the total number of pets is\n\n\\[\n15+f+\\frac{f}{3}=15+\\frac{4f}{3}.\n\\]\n\nAt \\$6 per package, Larry spends\n\n\\[\n6\\left(15+\\frac{4f}{3}\\right)=90+8f.\n\\]\n\nSince the number of fish is not given, the total cost cannot be determined uniquely.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$90+8f\\text{, where }f\\text{ is the number of fish}}\n\\]",
    "Interpreting your latest correction as replacing “Larry has 3 cats,” Larry has:\n\n- \\(4\\) cats\n- \\(3 \\times 4 = 12\\) dogs\n\nIf Larry has \\(f\\) fish, then he has \\(\\frac{f}{3}\\) gerbils. Thus, the total number of pets is\n\n\\[\n4+12+f+\\frac{f}{3}\n=16+\\frac{4f}{3}.\n\\]\n\nAt \\$6 per package, the total cost is\n\n\\[\n6\\left(16+\\frac{4f}{3}\\right)=96+8f.\n\\]\n\nBecause the number of fish is not specified, a numerical total cannot be determined.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$96+8f\\text{, where }f\\text{ is the number of fish}}\n\\]",
    "Larry has:\n\n- \\(4\\) cats\n- \\(3 \\times 4 = 12\\) dogs\n- \\(12-2=10\\) rabbits\n- \\(f\\) fish\n- \\(\\frac{f}{3}\\) gerbils\n\nSo the total number of pets is\n\n\\[\n4+12+10+f+\\frac{f}{3}\n=26+\\frac{4f}{3}.\n\\]\n\nAt \\$6 per package, Larry spends\n\n\\[\n6\\left(26+\\frac{4f}{3}\\right)=156+8f.\n\\]\n\nSince the number of fish is still not given, the total cannot be determined numerically.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$156+8f\\text{, where }f\\text{ is the number of fish}}\n\\]",
    "Larry has \\(4\\) cats and \\(3\\) times as many dogs:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 4 = 12 \\text{ dogs}\n\\]\n\nHe has 2 fewer rabbits than dogs:\n\n\\[\n12-2=10\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{10\\text{ rabbits}}\n\\]",
    "Larry has:\n\n- \\(4\\) cats\n- \\(3 \\times 4 = 12\\) dogs\n- \\(12-2=10\\) rabbits\n- \\(3 \\times 10=30\\) fish\n- \\(\\frac{30}{3}=10\\) gerbils\n\nTotal pets:\n\n\\[\n4+12+10+30+10=66\n\\]\n\nAt \\$6 per package:\n\n\\[\n66 \\times 6=\\boxed{\\$396}\n\\]",
